<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" ?>
<Defs>
  <!--
    Templated from VFEP's VFEP_WarcasketShoulders_Siegebreaker (VFEP v3.09,
    1.6/Defs/ThingDefs_Misc/Apparel_Various.xml); fields not discussed here are Siegebreaker's.
    Plating, tags and the market-value references follow the armor's header, as do the art and
    tint-mask notes. Siegebreaker's EnergyShieldRechargeRate offset is not copied: it is a
    thing-level stat, so an offset on a pawn's apparel never reaches the armor's shield.

    Tuning: ComponentSpacer 2 / Plasteel 60 / MedicineIndustrial 2 (Siegebreaker 0 / 60). The
    plasteel is the 10th-gen shoulder-to-armor ratio, roughly 0.4 (Siegebreaker 60/145,
    Guardian 80/200, Controller 60/150, Sarcophagus 60/145, Brute 60/160), of the armor's 145.
    The components are the Controller shoulders' price for a verb, here the injector. The
    medicine is the injector's full first fill, two shots, on the armor's terms. 976 silver at
    market value.

    The medic offsets:
    - MedicalTendSpeed +0.25, about four Medicine levels on vanilla's skill curve for that stat;
      reaches the mechanite dressing through vanilla's tend formula and a normal tend alike.
    - No capacity floor: the tier's 0.7 Manipulation floor is on every VFEP armor already, and
      a 1.0 floor is Sarcophagus's identity, left to that set's pieces for a mix-and-match
      pilot who wants it. The speed offset and the injector are the pads' whole function.

    Adrenaline shot: VEF CompAbilitiesApparel grants MDWC_AdrenalineShot (AbilityDefs/
    AdrenalineShot.xml), fed by the injector beside it, a plain vanilla CompApparelReloadable
    the ability reads off the apparel that grants it, so both comps sit on this one def (the
    Aerial shoulders' pairing). ammoCountPerCharge 1: one item loads one shot. With it set,
    vanilla's NeedsReload is remaining != max on both the idle and the forced path, so
    colonists fetch an item for every empty slot, and ReloadFrom adds min(stack / perCharge,
    max - remaining), so a forced reload never discards anything. Refill mode
    (ammoCountToRefill) is not used: a multi-shot refill item leaves the pilot on its last
    shot until empty or throws the remainder away on an early reload, while a per-item charge
    has no remainder. The per-fight budget is the loaded count, since a drafted pilot cannot
    reload: maxCharges 2 makes each shot a decision mid-fight, with a loot of a downed raider's
    medicine the only way to recharge it before the fight ends. ammoDef MedicineIndustrial:
    adrenaline is epinephrine, a cardiac drug drawn from a medical kit, which fits the
    heart-attack rule, and an industrial kit is 18 silver at market value. ammoDef and
    maxCharges are mod settings defaulting to these values; the ammo setting also writes the
    item's uiIcon onto the ability as its placeholder art. The free first fill is two
    industrial kits, the costList's MedicineIndustrial 2.
    chargeNoun "shot": the inspect line, the stat sheet and the empty message count in shots.
    No verbs, so the comp draws no gizmo of its own; the ability's command shows the count.
    Its DefInjected keys read comps.CompApparelReloadable, the vanilla comp class.

    ApparelExtension priority 1, for the reason in the armor def's header: the
    VFEP_WarcasketShoulderPadBase parent carries its own, and only the highest-priority copy
    keeps its fields whole (Merge still ORs the parent's isUnifiedApparel in). Any new
    ApparelExtension field for this piece goes on this entry.

    Compat: SOS2Patch.xml and the VGE vacuum patch leave shoulder pads alone, as VFEP's and
    VGE1's own patches do for VFEP's. The 1.6/Mods/CombatExtended/Patches/ root rescales the
    plating and adds bulk, as CE's does for VFEP's.
  -->
  <VFEPirates.WarcasketDef ParentName="VFEP_WarcasketShoulderPadBase">
    <defName>MDWC_WarcasketShoulders_Medic</defName>
    <label>medic warcasket shoulders</label>
    <shortDescription>Specialized spacer-tech warcasket pauldrons with standard protection, fitted with field-medicine manipulators that quicken the pilot's tending and an adrenaline injector.</shortDescription>
    <description>Specialized spacer-tech warcasket pauldrons with standard protection, fitted with field-medicine manipulators that quicken the pilot's tending and an adrenaline injector.\n\nA 10th-generation design from the government program that rebuilt captured pirate rigs around its own power armor and gave them to veterans who could no longer serve any other way. The Medic was its rig for the surgeons who had served beside them.\n\nThe shell's dressing suite tends a squadmate's wounds where they fall, the pauldrons' injector keeps them on their feet for a few hours more, and the helmet's visor diagnoses what no bandage treats. Plating and shield are the generation's standard, so a Medic fights a step behind the line, and a squad that fields one holds out long after its bandages would have run out.</description>
    <graphicData>
      <texPath>Things/Pawn/Warcasketlike/WarcasketMedic/WarcasketMedicShoulders</texPath>
      <shaderType>CutoutComplex</shaderType>
    </graphicData>
    <statBases>
      <Mass>20</Mass>
      <ArmorRating_Sharp>2</ArmorRating_Sharp>
      <ArmorRating_Blunt>1</ArmorRating_Blunt>
      <ArmorRating_Heat>1</ArmorRating_Heat>
      <Insulation_Cold>22</Insulation_Cold>
      <Insulation_Heat>22</Insulation_Heat>
      <EquipDelay>1</EquipDelay>
    </statBases>
    <equippedStatOffsets>
      <SlaveSuppressionOffset MayRequire="Ludeon.RimWorld.Ideology">0.2</SlaveSuppressionOffset>
      <MedicalTendSpeed>0.25</MedicalTendSpeed>
      <VacuumResistance MayRequire="Ludeon.RimWorld.Odyssey">0.1</VacuumResistance>
    </equippedStatOffsets>
    <costList>
      <ComponentSpacer>2</ComponentSpacer>
      <Plasteel>60</Plasteel>
      <MedicineIndustrial>2</MedicineIndustrial>
    </costList>
    <researchPrerequisites>
      <li>VFEP_SpacerWarcaskets</li>
    </researchPrerequisites>
    <apparel>
      <bodyPartGroups>
        <li>Shoulders</li>
        <li>Arms</li>
        <li>Hands</li>
        <li>Neck</li>
      </bodyPartGroups>
      <wornGraphicPath>Things/Pawn/Warcasketlike/WarcasketMedic/WarcasketMedicShoulders</wornGraphicPath>
      <useWornGraphicMask>true</useWornGraphicMask>
      <layers>
        <li>OnSkin</li>
        <li>Middle</li>
        <li>Shell</li>
      </layers>
      <tags>
        <li>WarcasketVeteran</li>
        <li>WarcasketAll</li>
      </tags>
    </apparel>
    <comps>
      <li Class="CompProperties_ApparelReloadable">
        <maxCharges>2</maxCharges>
        <ammoDef>MedicineIndustrial</ammoDef>
        <ammoCountPerCharge>1</ammoCountPerCharge>
        <baseReloadTicks>60</baseReloadTicks>
        <soundReload>Standard_Reload</soundReload>
        <chargeNoun>shot</chargeNoun>
      </li>
      <li Class="VEF.Abilities.CompProperties_AbilitiesApparel">
        <abilities>
          <li>MDWC_AdrenalineShot</li>
        </abilities>
      </li>
    </comps>
    <modExtensions>
      <li Class="VEF.Apparels.ApparelExtension">
        <priority>1</priority>
      </li>
    </modExtensions>
  </VFEPirates.WarcasketDef>
</Defs>
